                <pb facs="0196" n="184" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg184"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">845.00/1776: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. William Phillips, Personal Representative of
                        President Roosevelt in India, to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New Delhi</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-01-27T19:00:00+06:30">January 27, 1943—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 28—7:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>87. I had my first long talk with the Viceroy with regard to Indian affairs last
                    evening during which I expressed the interest of the <pb facs="0197" n="185"
                        xml:id="pg185"/> Americans in seeing a settlement of India’s problems. I
                    told His Excellency that I had been receiving Indians from many walks of life
                    and different political opinions in an effort to understand their problems. I
                    explained the purpose of my projected visits to various parts of the country
                    where I hoped to obtain further enlightenment. The Viceroy cordially approved of
                    my plans and assured me that on my return to Delhi he would go over the entire
                    situation with me in detail. In reply to my inquiry as to whether in his opinion
                    there was any possibility of his reopening the discussions with the Indian
                    leaders he indicated that he stood ready to do so but of course under certain
                    conditions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
